  "body": "## Report from the maintainer\n\nThe maintainer said that the \"Export Agie inspection setup\" text and button \"appear everywhere\". Agie-only controls must show only for a job for the Agie control (AGIECUT CLASSIC 2S, the native Agie post).\n\n## What showed where, and why\n\n| Place | Before | Cause |\n|---|---|---|\n| Post page of a setup, section \"Agie nominal inspection\" (`agie_inspection.rs`) | Shown for each setup. On another machine it said \"Mount the AGIECUT CLASSIC 2S machine on this setup ...\". | The section returned early only when there was no setup AND no Agie machine. |\n| Operation page, action \"Export Agie inspection setup\" and the hint \"Nominal inspection only ...\" (`op_page.rs`) | Shown on each normal DXF die cut, on each machine. | `has_agie_inspection_source` is true for each active die-side Wire Contour on one DXF sketch chain. It does not read the machine. |\n| Wire page, open cut (Left/Right), rows \"Both pieces clamped through all passes\", \"Stock centered in installed XY travel\" and the hint \"Agie open cuts require ...\" (`wire_page.rs`) | Shown for each post. | Only the native Agie post reads the two flags (`agie_profile.rs`). |\n\nOther places were checked. The post dialog already shows its Agie rows only for the native Agie post (`posting::agie::is_native`). `browser_files.rs` only maps `ImportAgieDrawing` and `ExportAgieInspection` to browser refusals; the only UI that starts them is the Post page section and the operation action. The File and Import menus have no Agie item. MCP is not changed.\n\n## The rule and the change\n\n- `agie_mounted(world, ctx)`: the setup context mounts the AGIECUT CLASSIC 2S machine of the wire EDM kind. This is the same test that `prepare_inspection` uses for the export.\n- `agie_job(world, ctx)`: `agie_mounted`, or the setup context posts with the native Agie post.\n- The Post page section (and its \"Import DXF drawing\" button) draws only when `agie_mounted`. The \"Mount the AGIECUT ...\" hint is removed.\n- The export action and its \"Nominal inspection only\" hint show only when `has_agie_inspection_source` is true and the operation's own setup is `agie_mounted`.\n- The Wire page open-cut rows and hint show only when `agie_job`.\n\nFor an Agie setup, nothing changes: the section, the import, the export and the rows show as before. No command, MCP tool, project field or name changes. Decision record: `docs/decisions/3996-agie-only-ui.md`.\n\nThe rename of the Agie post and its texts is tracked in #4000. This PR renames nothing and keeps the present wording of each Agie text.\n\n## Pinning tests (`camcraft-ui` lib)\n\nRed on `main` d80dc6944 first (run on winbuild), green on this head:\n- `egui_app::op_page::agie_inspection_tests::plain_dxf_wire_cut_on_another_machine_shows_no_agie_export` (red on main: \"no Agie export on a non-Agie job\")\n- `egui_app::op_page::agie_inspection_tests::non_agie_setup_post_page_has_no_agie_inspection_section` (red on main)\n- `egui_app::wire_page::tests::open_cut_hides_the_agie_statements_for_another_wire_post` (red on main: \"Both pieces clamped through all passes shows for a non-Agie post\")\n- `egui_app::tests::page_layout::layout_page_setup_post` (new assertion: no Agie section on a non-Agie setup)\n\nAgie behaviour kept:\n- `agie_setup_post_page_keeps_the_agie_inspection_section`, `agie_inspection_opening_still_shows_its_export` (new)\n- `saved_selected_opening_exports_zero_steps_through_the_desktop_action`, `setup_post_inspection_fields_and_submit_fit_the_visible_panel`, `unassigned_inspection_opening_survives_undo_redo_and_project_reopen` (unchanged)\n- `the_open_cutoff_declarations_apply_and_undo_together` now selects the native Agie post first, because the rows are Agie-only.\n\nThe `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by 5. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild)\n\nLog `C:\\camcraft-logs\\gate-3996-60aac6c98.log`. Branch head `60aac6c98803e49687de59c57b920729baa6036d`. `origin/main` was `d80dc6944`, so the gated tree is the branch head.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (`CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`): 10 of 10 steps ok. `ui suites: lib`: 1663 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: exit 0.\n- `camcraft-app` is not changed, so no app clippy.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nSynthetic wire ISO fixture machine, a DXF notch, shell 1600 x 1100. Before: `main` d80dc6944. After: head 60aac6c98.\n\n| View | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Post page of a setup on another wire machine | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3996/before-post-page-non-agie-setup.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3996/after-post-page-non-agie-setup.png) |\n| Normal DXF die cut on another wire machine | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3996/before-dxf-wire-op-page.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3996/after-dxf-wire-op-page.png) |\n| Wire page, open cut (Left), Fanuc post | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3996/before-wire-page-open-cut.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3996/after-wire-page-open-cut.png) |\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The browser (wasm) build: the change is in the shared page code and adds no browser path.\n- The hover hints: the form helper draws a hint as the hover text of the row above it, so the tests assert the rows and the action, not the hint text.\n- No light-lane or heavy step: no post, toolpath or geometry code changes.\n\nChangelog: Agie-only controls (the nominal inspection section, the inspection export action and the open-cut clamp statements) now show only for a setup on the Agie machine or with the native Agie post.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3996\n",
